  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Exercise Book",
    "overview": "**Creative North Star: \"The Exercise Book\"**\n\nMoney kept the way a Jamaican household always kept it: on paper, in a school exercise book. Every screen is a page with a red double margin rule down the left, dates written in that margin, words written to the right of it, and sums lined up in the right-hand column. Goals are the books themselves: solid card covers in blue, purple, teal, plum, indigo or slate, each with a white label plate filled in NAME and BY. Ink is ballpoint navy on off-white paper. There is no chrome to speak of; structure comes from rules, not boxes.\n\nThe system deliberately refuses the finance-app default of tonal Material cards, a donut chart and wallpaper-driven dynamic colour. Material 3 supplies behaviour (navigation bar, sheets, chips, buttons, snackbars); the Exercise Book supplies every colour role, the type scale and the shapes. Density is generous and one-handed: rows are at least 64px tall, primary actions are 56px tall, and the quick-add keypad sits at the bottom of the screen.\n\nThe night book is the same book with the lights off: a deep navy page, pale ink, and label plates that turn dark rather than staying white, because the night status colours are tuned light for a dark ground and would fail on white.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Red double margin rule at 56px on every ruled page; margin holds dates, the writing starts at 68px.",
      "Each ledger line sits on its own feint blue rule, amount right-aligned in the sum column.",
      "Totals close under a short double ink rule.",
      "Goal = solid exercise-book cover + white NAME / BY label plate; cover hue never carries status.",
      "Status says itself three ways: colour, icon plus word, and rule form (solid, dashed, double).",
      "One typeface, Atkinson Hyperlegible Next, with tabular figures on every amount.",
      "One extended FAB, \"Spend\", opens keypad-first quick add."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Covers Are Not Signals Rule",
        "body": "Cover hues avoid green, amber and red entirely. Status colour appears only on the status line, a limit warning or an amount, never as a cover.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Night Plate Rule",
        "body": "In the night book the label and status plates are `night-label-plate`, not white. Light-tuned status colours on a white plate would lose contrast.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Red Line Rule",
        "body": "Margin red belongs to the margin. Anything that is actually wrong uses status-behind.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Four Sums Rule",
        "body": "Every amount prints at one of four sizes: hero (44/800), large (26/700), row (17/700), small (15/600). Pick by the job the figure does, never by the space available; a figure that does not fit shrinks to fit its column rather than wrapping or picking a new size.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Figures Rule",
        "body": "Every amount and every display-size figure uses tabular figures so columns of money line up.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Ruled, Not Raised Rule",
        "body": "Separate things with a rule (feint for rows, ink for totals, margin red for the margin), never with a shadow or a tonal card.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** put every page's content inside the ruled page, starting at the 68px writing inset with dates in the 56px margin.",
      "**Do** end every ledger line on its own feint rule and put its amount in the right-hand sum column.",
      "**Do** close totals under the double ink rule.",
      "**Do** say status three ways at once: status colour, icon plus word, and rule form (solid, dashed, double).",
      "**Do** size money only from the four-step amount ramp (hero, large, row, small) with tabular figures, and let a figure shrink to fit rather than wrap.",
      "**Do** give each goal a cover from the six cover hues, chosen stably from its id, with a NAME / BY label plate.",
      "**Do** use dark label and status plates in the night book.",
      "**Do** keep quick add keypad-first: type the amount, tap a category, saved."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** use tonal Material cards, surface tint or shadows to group content; use rules.",
      "**Don't** draw a donut or pie chart; spending is horizontal bars with their own labels.",
      "**Don't** turn on dynamic (wallpaper) colour; the palette is fixed.",
      "**Don't** colour a goal cover green, amber or red, or use a cover hue to signal status.",
      "**Don't** use margin red for errors or warnings.",
      "**Don't** show status by colour alone.",
      "**Don't** introduce a second typeface or a mono face for numbers."
